WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:01.134 line:92%
-According to some polls,

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:03.303 size:81% position:41%
you are the top choice
for Democratic voters

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
as far as who
they would like to see

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:07.540 line:92%
as a vice presidential choice.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that something
that would interest you?

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you had any conversations
about that?

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:15.815 size:81% position:41%
-So, I have not talked
with people about it.

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:19.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, I'm focused right no
on this crisis.

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:25.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
Last week, we were negotiating
the record $2 trillion bil

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:28.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
to try to support
healthcare workers

00:00:28.128 --> 00:00:29.629 line:92%
and try to support our economy

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:32.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now I'm pushing hard
on this oversight part of it

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:35.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
sending these letters, for
example, to Secretary Mnuchin.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:38.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's just where my attention
is focused right now.

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:40.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
Frankly, I think
it would be presumptuous

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:43.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
for me to be doing
anything else.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You haven't endorsed
a candidate yet.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:48.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it certainly seems lik
your positions line up

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
more in lockstep
with Senator Sanders

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.685 line:92%
than they do with Joe Biden.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:53.386 line:92%
Are you going to endorse,

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:56.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
or is this something
you're considering to wait on?

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, again,
I really just want to say,

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:03.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
right now, you know,
it's less about the politics

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:07.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
and much more about the crisis
that our country is in.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:11.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think that's really
where our focus has got to b

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:11.838 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at this moment.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:14.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, that's where I'm keeping
my attention right now.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:18.611
We don't get to do any political
rallies at this moment anyway.

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:22.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were asked about
gender's role in the campaig

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:23.950 size:81% position:41% line:92%
after you dropped out,

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you said
that it was a trap question.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.955
And the way you explained it
made a lot of sense to me.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:34.094
What steps do we have to take to
make it not be a trap question

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
for candidates like yourself
that run as women

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
in this country?
-Well, I'll tell you what,

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
let me just explain
the trap to everyone.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's, every time
you get asked the question

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Do you think you were
discriminated

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:45.672 size:88% position:44% line:92%
as a woman in this race?

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:49.876
Do you think it was harder
for you because you're a woman?"

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:51.144 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
My answer is, look,

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:52.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
any way I answer that,
we got a problem.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:58.685
If I say, "Yes, it was," then,
you know, you're just a whiner

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.687 line:92%
And if I say "No, it wasn't,

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
at least half the population
will say,

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What planet
does that woman live on?"

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:07.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you know, the best way
we can solve this is,

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:11.898
how about we elect a woman
President sometime soon?

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.600 line:92%
And then we break that ceiling

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.070 size:88% position:44%
and we don't have to ask
that question so often.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.072 size:88% position:44%
-I think that would be
a nice solution to that.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:20.306 line:92%
I have talked to you in the past

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
about Kate McKinnon's
portrayal of you.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:26.846 size:88% position:44%
You finally got a chance
to be on-stage with her

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:27.547 line:92%
at "Saturday Night Live."

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:30.950
How was -- hopefully not the
last "Saturday Night Live" ever.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:34.053 size:88% position:44%
It is currently the last
"Saturday Night Live."

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:36.356 line:92%
How was that experience for you?

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.858 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-It was so much fun.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:41.194 size:78% position:39%
I mean, Kate McKinnon
is just wonderful.

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:43.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's such an incredibly
talented comedian.

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:47.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I have to tell,
what was even more fun is,

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.502 size:84% position:42% line:92%
a couple of days later,

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:53.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was at the grocery store
at our Shaw's market.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:56.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one of the workers
at the grocery store came up

00:02:56.876 --> 00:03:00.914
this lady, and she looks and
sees me in the checkout line

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:05.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she says, "People,
we've got a celebrity here!"

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:06.352 line:92%
And everybody looks around

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:09.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she says,
"It's Kate McKinnon!"

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.957 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:15.028
-I can't believe you didn'
count as a celebrity until that.

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:15.962 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
She got it exactly right.

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:21.267 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I heard rumors,

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you can tell me
if it's true,

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.971 line:92%
that between dress and air

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:27.674
which is one of the most fraught
times at "SNL,"

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:28.441 line:92%
you actually made the case

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:32.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
for some of the lines
to not be cut from the sketch.

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:34.781 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I did. [ Laughs ]

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:38.685 line:92%
I did, Including the one about

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:42.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I didn't die. I'm just
in the United States Senate.

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:43.289 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:44.624 line:92%
-There you go. I can tell you,

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:47.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
having worked there and having
been a writer on the show,

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:48.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the writers
who wrote those lines,

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:51.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
the fact that you
fought for them,

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:54.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
they will be fans
of yours forever.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.769 line:92%
-And I will be fans of theirs.

